<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Giovanni Paolo Lascaris</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1560">1560</a>–<a href="/years/1657">1657</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Jean-Paul de Lascaris-Castellar</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Giovanni Paolo Lascaris was Grand Master of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/knights-hospitaller">Knights Hospitaller</a> from 1636 to 1657, one of the longest reigns in the order's history. He strengthened the fortifications of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/malta">Malta</a> and in 1651 approved the purchase of French <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caribbean">Caribbean</a> islands, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-kitts">Saint Kitts</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-croix">Saint Croix</a>, which the order held until 1665. He died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/valletta">Valletta</a> in 1657, in his late nineties.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/giovanni-paolo-lascaris.jpg" alt="Giovanni Paolo Lascaris" width="320" height="409" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Carlo F. Polizzi · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Giovanni_Paolo_Lascaris_di_Ventimiglia_e_Castellar.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
